{"name":"Vivid Malachite","hex":"#00cc33","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vivid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Clear, detailed, or powerful.","Bright, intense, or colourful."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A felt-tipped permanent marker; a marker pen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vivid"},{"term":"malachite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bright green mineral, a basic copper carbonate, Cu2CO3(OH)2; one of the principal ores of copper.","A mild green color, like that of the mineral."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a color ranging from olive-taupe to a mild to deeply-rich (at times seemingly translucent) green, like that of the mineral which is present on oxidized copper."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/malachite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Malachite","blocks":[{"text":"Malachite is a copper carbonate hydroxide mineral, with the formula Cu2CO3(OH)2. This opaque, green-banded mineral crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system, and most often forms botryoidal, fibrous, or stalagmitic masses, in fractures and deep, underground spaces, where the water table and hydrothermal fluids provide the means for chemical precipitation. Individual crystals are rare, but occur as slender to acicular prisms. Pseudomorphs after more tabular or blocky azurite crystals also occur."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Malachite%2C_Zaire.jpg/330px-Malachite%2C_Zaire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malachite","wikidata":"Q164411"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a green or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Shades_of_Green.svg/330px-Shades_of_Green.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_green","wikidata":"Q19847180"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Great_Orme_Copper_Mine_-_geograph.org.uk_-_819.jpg/500px-Great_Orme_Copper_Mine_-_geograph.org.uk_-_819.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Great_Orme_Copper_Mine_-_geograph.org.uk_-_819.jpg/500px-Great_Orme_Copper_Mine_-_geograph.org.uk_-_819.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The entrance to the Neolithic era malachite mine complex on the Great Orme, Wales","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreat_Orme_Copper_Mine_-_geograph.org.uk_-_819.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Outokumpu_malachite.jpg/500px-Outokumpu_malachite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Outokumpu_malachite.jpg/1280px-Outokumpu_malachite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Outokumpu_malachite.jpg/500px-Outokumpu_malachite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Malachite in the walls of Outokumpu's old mine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOutokumpu_malachite.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Malachite_001.png/120px-Malachite_001.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Malachite_001.png/250px-Malachite_001.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten